Synthesis:
In Wrangler, Cloudflare D1 tracks applied SQL migration files (from your migrations_dir) in the d1_migrations table inside the D1 database; by default this table is named d1_migrations and it records each migration’s filename (name) plus applied_at (and an id). You can change both the tracking table and the migrations folder in wrangler.{jsonc|toml} under d1_databases using migrations_table and migrations_dir. Wrangler commands are wrangler d1 migrations list/apply <database_name>. [1][2][3]

